# Open Brain — Encrypted offsite backup cron entry (Unraid host)
#
# INSTALLED 2026-06-11 (Entry 164, arch-review v3 RC-1). Kept for reference/rebuild.
#
# INSTALL (once, after a homeserver rebuild):
#   1. SSH to homeserver as `root` (/boot/config is root-only readable).
#   2. Append the cron line below (with its comment) to:
#        /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron
#   3. Reload cron: /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
#   4. Verify: grep offsite-backup /etc/cron.d/root
#   5. Recreate the [open-brain-offsite] crypt remote in
#      /mnt/user/appdata/rclone-onedrive/config/rclone.conf if missing —
#      see docs/runbooks/offsite-backup.md (password + salt in BWS).
#
# SCHEDULE: daily 03:45 — after backup.sh (03:00, takes <10 min) writes the
#   new daily dir. Slot audited 2026-06-11: 45 3 * * * is free across host
#   crons (0 3 backup, 0 3,15 rclone-onedrive, 0 4,16 rclone-gdrive) and
#   BullMQ scheduler slots (Sunday 0 3 / 30 3 / 0 4 / 0 5).
#
# ROLLBACK:
#   sed -i '/offsite-backup/d' /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/custom.cron
#   /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
#   Remote data persists until manually deleted (rclone purge open-brain-offsite:).
#
# LOGS: /var/log/open-brain-offsite-backup.log
#
# PUSHOVER: failure alert (priority 1) via scripts/lib/pushover-notify.sh —
#   cron line sources .env.secrets (set -a) for PUSHOVER_APP_TOKEN/USER_KEY.

45 3 * * * cd /mnt/user/appdata/open-brain && bash -c 'set -a; . ./.env.secrets 2>/dev/null; set +a; bash scripts/offsite-backup.sh' >> /var/log/open-brain-offsite-backup.log 2>&1
